3. Distribute your derivative works, free of charge or alongside other free projects.

[Conditions] Provided that you:

1. Attribution
   Any derivative work or redistributed copy MUST keep at least one credit to the
   original author inside the source code. Copy this line into a file header:

       Based on dsh-at-plugins by thynon — https://github.com/thynon/dsh-at-plugins

   A note in the README or documentation alone does not satisfy this; it must live
   in a code file.

2. No charging
   You may not charge for this project or any derivative of it without the author's
   prior written permission. This includes selling, paid downloads, paywalls,
   subscriptions, per-use or per-time billing, and bundling into a paid product or
   paid service.

3. Same license
   Derivative works must remain under this license. You may not relicense them under
   a more permissive license (for example, you may not switch back to MIT or
   Apache-2.0). You may add stricter terms on top.

4. Keep the notice
   Redistributions must retain this LICENSE file unchanged, together with the
   existing copyright and attribution notices in the source.

